{"cluster_id": "C-1885", "topic": "The orphan-sweep watermark floor is derived from the namespace's own pre", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B046-064"], "canonical_claim": "The orphan-sweep watermark floor is derived from the namespace's own prefix segments and a live mount lease; a namespace rooted outside the pool's server_root_id is permanently ineligible for sweeping regardless of epoch or coverage.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t4-report.md#L121-L136", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t4-review.md#L146-L150"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1886", "topic": "After probe-A deletion, `Gc", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-035", "B047-001", "B047-003"], "canonical_claim": "After probe-A deletion, `Gc::RefScanSummary` retains `changed_shards`, `keys`, `listed_lives`, `logs_by_life`, and `max_log_by_life` because each field has consumers outside `sampleRefListQuality`.; Probe A is deleted because catalog-authoritative discovery and LIST-independent recovery make its second full stream LIST irrelevant to correctness; B1/B2 accounting and the mount-time capability probe remain.; T5 removes `Gc::sampleRefListQuality` and its `ref_list_probe` call, so a regular GC round no longer performs a second full ref-prefix LIST for store-quality sampling.", "issue_ids": ["R7", "T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t5-draft-report.md#L15-L29", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t5-draft-report.md#L31-L38", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-ref-rework-adjacent-findings.md#r7-probe-a-gating", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-7a"]}
