{"cluster_id": "C-1888", "topic": "When the graduation or redelete budget is exhausted, `settleEntry` carri", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-004", "B011-021", "B048-020"], "canonical_claim": "When the graduation or redelete budget is exhausted, `settleEntry` carries the entry in `still_retired` unchanged: a condemned entry remains condemned, and a `delete_pending` entry remains `delete_pending` for a later round.; Retired-in-snapshot preserves settlement semantics including condemn, carry, round-paced graduation, `delete_pending`, redelete, clamp suppression, the pre-CAS single delete site, resurrect-supersede, `.meta` writes, B170 events, and GC-log counters.; The two-cursor merge settles a pending row by exact-token redelete at d = 0, spares any row at d > 0, graduates a nonpending row when `condemn_round < current_round`, and otherwise carries it unchanged.", "issue_ids": ["B170", "T6-2"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L25-L60", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#merge", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#problem"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1889", "topic": "One GcRoundWorkBudget is constructed per round", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B048-021"], "canonical_claim": "One `GcRoundWorkBudget` is constructed per round in `Gc::runRegularRound` and shared by sequential shard folds; it is passed to all production `foldDeltasIntoGeneration` calls, while the rebuild path remains unbudgeted because it has no graduation or `delete_pending` inputs.", "issue_ids": ["T6-2"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L25-L60"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1890", "topic": "deletePrefixWholesale reports out_fully_drained true only when", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B048-028"], "canonical_claim": "`deletePrefixWholesale` reports `out_fully_drained = true` only when the LIST reaches its natural end; budget exhaustion reports false, and `pruneSupersededGenerations` advances `snap_pruned_through` only past fully drained prefixes.", "issue_ids": ["T6-3"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L200-L220"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1891", "topic": "The post CAS generation prefix hand", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B048-030"], "canonical_claim": "The post-CAS generation-prefix hand-off uses a separate budget from ordinary prune work because it is a one-shot event whose only existing backstop after a partial reclaim is `fsck`.", "issue_ids": ["C4"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L220-L236", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L434-L482"]}

